    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0259" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/978.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Chinese Government has reduced the amount of the proposed loan to
                    £10,000,000, expecting relaxation of supervision. The British Minister informs
                    me however that his Government refuses to relax the conditions even for the
                    reduced amount. Similar information as to the attitude of the French
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
